{"ClientSettings":{"Pn":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"P"},"Sc":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"H"},"Qz":{"Cn":1,"St":0,"Qs":0,"Prod":"T"},"Ap":true,"Mute":true,"Lad":"2026-11-28T00:00:00Z","Iotd":0,"Gwb":0,"Tns":0,"Dft":null,"Mvs":0,"Flt":0,"Imp":1,"Tobn":0},"MediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"This autumnal view from Letná Park looks out over Prague, which grew up along the banks of the Vltava River in Czechia. In today's image, the river winds its way through the historic Old Town and Malá Strana districts, beneath Mánes Bridge in the foreground. Many beautiful bridges now span the Vltava, but for centuries there was only one, Charles Bridge, pictured second from the bottom. Its first stones were laid in 1357 during the reign of Charles IV and until 1841, it was the only way to cross the river on foot. Today its stone arches, gothic towers and statues lining the bridge draw large crowds, so tourists are advised to get there by dawn for the best photographs. Or they could walk on to the next crossing, Legion Bridge, which is less crowded and offers beautiful views of the National Theatre, Prague Castle and its busier neighbour.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.VltavaPrague_EN-IN7319350687_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.VltavaPrague_EN-IN7319350687_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Bridges through time","Title":"Old town and Vltava River, Prague, Czechia","Copyright":"© Lara_Uhryn/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/50.089959,14.412867/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=50.089959,14.412867;S9;Mánes Bridge, Prague&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261128_VltavaPrague\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Prague+bridges&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261127_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261128_VltavaPrague"},"Ssd":"20261128","Name":"VltavaPrague","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7319350687","FullDateString":"28 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Hidden within an ancient sandstone landscape, Face Canyon is one of 96 canyons stretching out from Lake Powell in southern Utah. Many are far from roads and would be hard to reach if they hadn't been flooded by the lake, created in 1963 during the construction of the Glen Canyon Dam. The lake's waters back up about 300 kilometres, along creeks and canyons which you can explore by boat, kayak or personal watercraft.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FaceCanyon_EN-IN7727815834_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FaceCanyon_EN-IN7727815834_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Ribbons of grey and gold","Title":"Butte at sunset, Face Canyon, Lake Powell, Utah, USA","Copyright":"© Jeff Foott/Minden","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/37.002262,-111.24176/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=37.002262,-111.24176;S9;Face Canyon, Utah&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261127_FaceCanyon\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Lake+Powell&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261126_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261127_FaceCanyon"},"Ssd":"20261127","Name":"FaceCanyon","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7727815834","FullDateString":"27 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Water, sunlight and lush greenery come together at Rainbow Falls in Hilo, on Hawaii's Big Island. Here, the Wailuku River plunges 24 metres over a lava ledge, sending mist into the air as it reaches the pool below. On sunny mornings, that mist can catch the light and produce the colourful rainbows that gave the falls their name. Known in Hawaiian as Waiānuenue, meaning 'rainbow water', this striking waterfall is surrounded by tropical vegetation and has a special place in Hawaiian legend.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.RFHilo_EN-IN3818497787_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.RFHilo_EN-IN3818497787_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Where rainbows fall","Title":"Rainbow Falls on the Wailuku River, Hilo, Hawaii, USA","Copyright":"© Peter Unger/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/19.718779,-155.108611/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=19.718779,-155.108611;S9;Rainbow Falls, Wailuku River&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261126_RFHilo\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Rainbow+Falls+Wailuku+River+Hawaii&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261125_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261126_RFHilo"},"Ssd":"20261126","Name":"RFHilo","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"3818497787","FullDateString":"26 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Snow transforms Bryce Canyon National Park, blanketing the landscape in white while its fiery orange-red hoodoos rise above the snowy terrain. Seen from Sunset Point, one of the park's most famous overlooks, these fantastical shapes are part of the Claron Formation, whose limestone was deposited about 50 million years ago and later shaped by weathering and erosion. Because much of the park rises above 2,400 metres, snow can arrive as early as October. In today's image, snow clings to the canyon's ridges and spires while mist drifts across the cliffs, creating an iconic winter scene in the American Southwest.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SunsetPoint_EN-IN8140664778_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SunsetPoint_EN-IN8140664778_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"When snow meets red rock","Title":"Sunset Point, Bryce Canyon National Park, Utah, USA","Copyright":"© Colin D. Young/Alamy","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/37.623535,-112.167279/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=37.623535,-112.167279;S9;Sunset Point, Bryce Canyon National Park, Utah&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261125_SunsetPoint\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Bryce+Canyon+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261124_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261125_SunsetPoint"},"Ssd":"20261125","Name":"SunsetPoint","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8140664778","FullDateString":"25 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As Britain's only native squirrel species, red squirrels thrive in Scotland's Cairngorms National Park. An important refuge, the park offers ancient Caledonian pine forests and newer conifer woodlands, with plentiful habitat and food for squirrels foraging for Scots pine seeds, nuts and other tasty morsels year-round. In today's image, a red squirrel is perched amid warm orange and yellow leaves, looking right at home as it ponders its next move in the Scottish Highlands.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.CairngormsSquirrel_EN-IN7928513964_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.CairngormsSquirrel_EN-IN7928513964_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Autumnal camouflage","Title":"Red squirrel in Cairngorms National Park, Highlands, Scotland","Copyright":"© Scotland: The Big Picture/Minden Pictures","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/57.0833,-3.6667/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=57.0833,-3.6667;S9;Cairngorms National Park, Highlands, Scotland&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261124_CairngormsSquirrel\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Eurasian+red+squirrel&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261123_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261124_CairngormsSquirrel"},"Ssd":"20261124","Name":"CairngormsSquirrel","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7928513964","FullDateString":"24 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Today's image shows the gradual coiling of a young fiddlehead's tip, echoing the geometric patterns seen throughout nature. In maths, the Fibonacci sequence follows a similar progression, each number formed by adding the two before it: 0, 1, 1, 2, 3, 5, 8 and so on. Today is Fibonacci Day, chosen for the numbers of the date (11/23) to honour the sequence. Eventually the young fern frond shown here will unfurl as it grows, but elsewhere in the plant world, the sequence will continue to appear in the spiralling arrangements of sunflower heads, pinecones, succulents and pineapples.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FibonacciFern_EN-IN6938090263_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FibonacciFern_EN-IN6938090263_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Geometry in nature","Title":"Fiddlehead fern","Copyright":"© Reza Saputra/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"The Fibonacci sequence was popularised through a 13th-century maths problem about multiplying rabbits.","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261123_FibonacciFern\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=fibonacci+day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261122_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261123_FibonacciFern"},"Ssd":"20261123","Name":"FibonacciFern","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"6938090263","FullDateString":"23 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Tucked into the cliffs of northern Spain's rugged coastline, the 16th-century Hermitage of Santa Justa, seen in today's image, overlooks the crashing waves of the Cantabrian Sea. Built partly into the rock and associated with relics of Saints Justa and Rufina, the small chapel eventually became a pilgrimage site, its sheltered stone walls creating a remarkable contrast with the powerful waves and rocky cliffs surrounding it.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.JustaHermitage_EN-IN3031288581_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.JustaHermitage_EN-IN3031288581_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Shelter among the waves","Title":"The chapel and hermitage of Santa Justa in Cantabria, Spain","Copyright":"© Tramont_ana/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/43.42595,-4.09762/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=43.42595,-4.09762;S9;Santa Justa, Cantabria&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261122_JustaHermitage\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Ermita+Santa+Justa+chapel&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261121_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261122_JustaHermitage"},"Ssd":"20261122","Name":"JustaHermitage","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"3031288581","FullDateString":"22 Nov, 2026"}],"PreloadMediaContents":[{"ImageContent":{"Description":"At Bowman's Beach, a tranquil canal winds through a lush coastal landscape. Mangroves thrive along the water's edge, stabilising the shoreline and filtering the water. Their intricate root systems create a valuable habitat for fish, alligators and the occasional manatee, while protecting shorelines from erosion, waves and storm surges. Their overhead branches host birds like osprey, herons and egrets. In today's image, the still canal reflects a wash of pink, purple and blue across the sky, creating a calm and colourful view of Florida's coast.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SanibelMangroves_EN-IN9001508760_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SanibelMangroves_EN-IN9001508760_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Life along the water's edge","Title":"Bowman's Beach Mangrove Canal, Sanibel Island, Florida","Copyright":"© Diana Robinson Photography/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/26.459567,-82.156509/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=26.459567,-82.156509;S9;Bowman's Beach, Sanibel Island, Florida&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261205_SanibelMangroves\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Bowmans+Beach+Mangrove+Canal+Sanibel+Island+Florida&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261204_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261205_SanibelMangroves"},"Ssd":"20261205","Name":"SanibelMangroves","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"9001508760","FullDateString":"5 Dec, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"As the world's fastest land animals, cheetahs are built for speed. Their slender bodies, semi-retractable claws and long legs and tails help with balance, traction and sharp turns. They can accelerate from 0 to 100 kilometres per hour in just a few seconds – faster than many sports cars. Cheetahs don't roar, instead communicating through chirps, purrs, growls and yelps and can be heard from kilometres away. As remarkable as cheetahs are, they're also one of the most endangered big cats in the world.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.CheetahLove_EN-IN8834942764_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.CheetahLove_EN-IN8834942764_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"A lasting spot in the wild","Title":"Cheetah female and cub, Samburu, Kenya","Copyright":"© Andy Rouse/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/1.321212,37.201945/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=1.321212,37.201945;S9;Samburu, Kenya&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261204_CheetahLove\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=international+cheetah+day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261203_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261204_CheetahLove"},"Ssd":"20261204","Name":"CheetahLove","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8834942764","FullDateString":"4 Dec, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Deep within Ranthambore National Park, Indian banyan trees take root. Unlike the trees that grow from the ground up, banyan seeds sprout on branches, buildings or ruins, dropped by passing birds. Once there, their aerial roots descend to the ground, slowly thickening into branch-supporting trunks. This allows the fig trees to spread over huge areas, providing fruit and shelter for wildlife and welcome shade for people.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.FicasBenghalensis_EN-IN8691619538_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.FicasBenghalensis_EN-IN8691619538_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Rooted in history","Title":"Indian banyan tree on arch ruin, Ranthambore National Park, India","Copyright":"© Vincent Grafhorst/Minden Pictures","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/27.304257,76.582332/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=27.304257,76.582332;S9;Ranthambore National Park&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261203_FicasBenghalensis\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Ranthambore+National+Park&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261202_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261203_FicasBenghalensis"},"Ssd":"20261203","Name":"FicasBenghalensis","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8691619538","FullDateString":"3 Dec, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"The fortress city of Valletta towers above the coast of Malta, surrounded by imposing walls rising out of the Mediterranean Sea. Founded in 1566, a year after the island country came under siege from the Ottoman Empire, it was built by the ruling knights of the Order of St John to ward off future invasions.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.ValettaSunrise_EN-IN8479375270_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.ValettaSunrise_EN-IN8479375270_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Dawn over Valletta","Title":"The historic city of Valletta, Malta","Copyright":"© RudyBalasko/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/35.898866,14.512414/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=35.898866,14.512414;S9;Valletta, Malta&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261202_ValettaSunrise\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=valletta+malta&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261201_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261202_ValettaSunrise"},"Ssd":"20261202","Name":"ValettaSunrise","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"8479375270","FullDateString":"2 Dec, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Who better to wish us a happy Antarctica Day than this waddle of emperor penguins, one of the frozen continent's most iconic species. While humans here are restricted to scientific research stations and expeditions, emperor penguins have learned to adapt to Antarctica's inhospitable climate. The emperors' dense feathers and fat reserves help to keep them warm. And this sociable bunch know how to share – they huddle together in groups, shuffling around so each gets a turn in the centre, where it's warmest.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.EmperorAntarctica_EN-IN7975920153_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.EmperorAntarctica_EN-IN7975920153_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Home of the emperors","Title":"Emperor penguins, Queen Maud Land, Antarctica","Copyright":"© Stefan Christmann/Nature Picture Library","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/-78.984829,75.491598/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=-78.984829,75.491598;S9;Antarctica&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261201_EmperorAntarctica\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Antarctica+Day&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261130_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261201_EmperorAntarctica"},"Ssd":"20261201","Name":"EmperorAntarctica","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7975920153","FullDateString":"1 Dec, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"We're looking out over one of Scotland's most otherworldly landscapes, formed by ancient landslides on the Isle of Skye. Millions of years ago, layers of heavy lava settled here on top of soft clay and rock, before gradually sliding down towards the sea. It left steep slopes, hidden plateaus and jagged rock formations along the Trotternish Peninsula, which forms Skye's northernmost tip.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.QuiraingSkye_EN-IN7608776732_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.QuiraingSkye_EN-IN7608776732_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Skye's sliding landscape","Title":"The Quiraing, Trotternish, Isle of Skye, Scotland","Copyright":"© Matt Anderson Photography/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/57.655679,-6.277862/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=57.655679,-6.277862;S9;The Quiraing, Skye, Scotland&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261130_QuiraingSkye\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=The+Quiraing+Isle+of+Skye+Scotland&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261129_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261130_QuiraingSkye"},"Ssd":"20261130","Name":"QuiraingSkye","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7608776732","FullDateString":"30 Nov, 2026"},{"ImageContent":{"Description":"Lit by streetlights as it crosses this narrow stretch of the Norwegian Sea, Sommarøy Bridge is the only road onto the small fishing island that shares its name. From a distance, with its white sand beaches and turquoise waters, you might think you were somewhere tropical. But Sommarøy sits north of the Arctic Circle and those are icy waters you're crossing.","Image":{"Url":"/th?id=OHR.SommaroyBridge_EN-IN7715485918_1920x1080.webp","Wallpaper":"/th?id=OHR.SommaroyBridge_EN-IN7715485918_1920x1200.jpg&rf=LaDigue_1920x1200.jpg","Downloadable":true},"Headline":"Skimming the sea","Title":"Sommarøy Bridge from above, Tromso, Norway","Copyright":"© Roberto Moiola/Sysaworld/Getty Images","SocialGood":null,"MapLink":{"Url":"//platform.bing.com/geo/REST/v1/Imagery/Map/RoadVibrant/69.623346,18.045599/5?key=AsSOKo7OOz5VAtfAj0rjgaXlhCrCZI6PGbLj7GCH8IW2HUalyg4BVhqA0z77PRCj&c=en-IN&od=2&shading=flat&pp=69.623346,18.045599;S9;Sommarøy Bridge, Norway&st=pp|v:false;lv:false_trs|v:false;lv:false&ml=Basemap,Landmarks&logo=no&mapSize=386,434&da=ro","Link":""},"QuickFact":{"MainText":"","LinkUrl":"","LinkText":""},"TriviaUrl":"/search?q=Bing+homepage+quiz&filters=WQOskey:\"HPQuiz_20261129_SommaroyBridge\"&FORM=HPQUIZ","BackstageUrl":"/search?q=Sommar%c3%b8y+Norway&form=hpcapt&filters=HpDate:\"20261128_1830\"+mgzv3configlist:\"BingQA_Encyclopedia_Layout\"","TriviaId":"HPQuiz_20261129_SommaroyBridge"},"Ssd":"20261129","Name":"SommaroyBridge","Market":"EN-IN","Hash":"7715485918","FullDateString":"29 Nov, 2026"}],"LocStrings":{"LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD":"दिन की छवि","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_IOTD_LEARN_MORE":"अधिक जानें","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_FACT":"त्वरित तथ्य:","LOC_HOMEPAGE_GALLERY_CARD_TITLE":"हाल ही की मुख पृष्ठ छवियाँ","LOC_HOMEPAGE_VERTICAL_SCROLL_GALLERY_IMAGE_ARIALABEL":"{0} की मुख्य पृष्ठ छवि","LOC_HOMEPAGE_ON_THIS_DAY_TITLE":"इतिहास में आज के